            "review_title": "Review at Japanese Restaurant Fuji",
            "review_text": "Mimimi2\nWashington DC, District of Columbia70 contributions\n1\nAvoid\nFeb 2019 • Friends\nThis was my most expensive meal in Vietnam and I’ve been staying at some exclusive resorts all over the country. I ordered finger clams and grilled vegetables which came out to around 800 VND. Rice was extra. Can you believe rice was 40 VND? Isn’t rice a staple part of Japanese meal? Finger clams were a total rip off. I couldn’t figure out where the clams were bc it was mostly seaweed and mushrooms. For a restaurant located in a 5 star hotel, it was disappointing. Also we waited at least 20-30 minutes to order. Vietnam has been so impressive with customer service that this is a total shock.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 26, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
