            "review_text": "Nahor\nLondon, United Kingdom39 contributions\n0\npricey teppanyaki but I could use the chopsticks\nJul 2015 • Family\nOur last day in Ho Chi Minh we decided to have a blow out in tnhe hotel Japanese restaurant, not sure how much of a blow out it would be! While all the courses were well design, prepared and served I felt the portion size were on the small side, especially the Japanese Wagyu Beef which whilst being the most delicious steak I have tasted could have been twice the size. The attention to detail was incredible the chopsticks had also been shipped from Japan which had been designed for easy use by novices. For 4 people the cost of the meal was equivalent to 5 nights at the Nikko Saigon.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 1, 2015",
