            "review_text": "Giulia Z\nDurham, United Kingdom115 contributions\n0\nGood food, bit pricey\nMay 2015 • Family\nA nice place no doubt, and we had some of the specials and the luxuries of watching the Japanese executive chef work some magic at the sushi counter. Very good, if a bit pricey. WARNING everywhere is smoking as Japanese culture demands it. But quite nice. Sashimi and sushi are great, tempura is not my style (everything is still juicy in the batter, which is the opposite of my tastes) and the wagyu beef was a lovely surprise.\nRead more\nWritten May 21, 2015",
