            "review_title": "Review at Japanese Restaurant Fuji",
            "review_text": "katanankes\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam90 contributions\n0\nFine Japanese dining, but probably not worth the premium\nMay 2015 • Solo\nI had a solo dinner at Fuji, in my quest to discover more options for Japanese in town. \n\nIn many way what I found was not unexpected, since Fuji Restaurant is located inside a five star hotel, Nikko, and follow the format of the five star hotel restaurant: an international chef (at least on paper), attentive but robotic staff, nice decor, but a bit \"glossy\" and with no much light...and of course an overpriced menu. it could honestly be in any five star hotel in town, \n\nThe menu boasts a large selection of sashimi, sushi, teppaniaky, some tempura and some seasfood extravaganza like a lobster meal. As expected, prices are twice as much of what you can pay in a normal restaurant for pretty much the same. \n\nI tried a sashimi and a sushi platter. I must say that I was favorably impressed by the fact that they did not try to shortchange me in the sushi mix and offered a number of high quality ingredients (i.e. scallop, red scallop, a tiny bit of sea urchin...). I also tried a small extravaganza: sushi with foi gras. I wish I could say it was delicious, but the foi gras was not that tasty (or maybe it was the combination).\n\nOverall I give this place a only a three star rating because the food is certainly fresh, qualitatively very good and well presented, but I do not see value for money and a distinctive value proposition or a particularly creative menu (with the exception of one or two dishes). I do not think I will come back, since I know already a number of places in which I can get much more for my buck. It could be an option for business luncheons or dinners since the place has a number of small private dining rooms. You can look at my reviews for a number of other sushi places in Saigon beyond the usual suspects.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 17, 2015",
